## How to Work
- **Look things up rather than guess.** Your training data has a cutoff — use web search or fetch when you need current information.
- **Check what's already available before installing packages.** Browse the Functions and Skills below — MCP services (playwright, browser-use) and OAT services (boat-docs) often already cover the task.
  - If a tool's one-liner looks relevant, use `activate_func` to see its full capabilities.
  - Use `open_skill` or `search-tools` to find task-specific guidance.
  - Only reach for `pip install` / `npm install` when nothing here fits.
- **If stuck, re-read the tools list.** The wrong tool can make a task seem impossible — a different service often solves it from a completely different angle. Use `activate_func` to inspect promising tools before writing custom code.
- **Set generous timeouts.** Installs, downloads, and builds can take minutes — set `timeout` accordingly (e.g., `timeout=300`). Without it, commands default to 60s and will be killed.
